replaceMission('5.5',0,'Six landform process cards','Waterfall: step/drop, undercutting and collapse. Gorge: steep-sided valley left as a waterfall retreats. Meander: bend migration. Oxbow lake: isolated cut-off bend. Floodplain: valley floor built partly by flood deposits. Natural levee: raised bank of deposited sediment.','Choose three cards: draw and explain one erosion feature, one bend feature and one deposition feature. Partners cover the other three, then teach each other.','Waterfall/gorge involve erosion and retreat; meander/oxbow involve erosion, deposition and cut-off; floodplain/levee involve flood deposition.');
replaceMission('5.5',1,'Landform guide challenge','A waterfall retreats upstream leaving a gorge. A meander neck narrows, a shorter channel breaks through, and deposits isolate the old bend. Floodwater deposits material on the floodplain; coarser material often settles near banks.','Storyboard the waterfall/gorge sequence and meander/oxbow sequence. Add a floodplain/levee diagram showing where sediment settles.','Label retreat and gorge behind the fall; neck narrowing, breakthrough and isolation; deposits near the banks can build natural levees.');
